cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If SurveyAtlas or the NavAtlas data helps your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SurveyAtlas: Living Literature Surveys for Fast-Moving Research Fields"
abstract: >-
  SurveyAtlas turns a research field's literature into a self-updating website: papers are harvested from arXiv
  and OpenAlex, classified into a field taxonomy by an LLM, linked to venues, citations and BibTeX, deep-read into
  structured notes with verified benchmark numbers, and served as a searchable library, a task-by-paradigm map,
  a timeline, benchmark leaderboards and a question-answering page. NavAtlas, the first atlas, covers
  vision-and-language navigation and embodied navigation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Xunyi
    alias: billzhao1030
repository-code: "https://github.com/billzhao1030/SurveyAtlas"
license: MIT
keywords:
